1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,690
Assalamu alaikum.

2
00:00:01,690 --> 00:00:06,499
We are team DecisionGuard, from the Bangladesh University of Professionals.

3
00:00:06,499 --> 00:00:10,538
DecisionGuard is a finance copilot for small Bangladeshi shops.

4
00:00:10,538 --> 00:00:16,885
It covers the three areas of Topic E: financing that fits, cash-flow alerts, and business analysis.

5
00:00:16,885 --> 00:00:19,450
One rule shapes everything you will see.

6
00:00:19,450 --> 00:00:27,528
Code computes every number, the language model only explains it, and nothing that matters happens until the owner approves it.

7
00:00:29,028 --> 00:00:32,183
The problem is the same in Dhaka and in Shenzhen.

8
00:00:32,183 --> 00:00:34,244
Small firms are short of credit.

9
00:00:34,244 --> 00:00:46,349
The IFC puts the gap at 5.7 trillion dollars across developing economies, and about 2.8 billion dollars in Bangladesh, where women-led firms get only 7.28 percent of small-business credit.

10
00:00:46,349 --> 00:00:55,622
And cash gets stuck: in a Peking University survey of over nine thousand Chinese small firms, 71 percent were owed money they had not been paid.

11
00:00:55,622 --> 00:01:01,932
Lenders say no because these shops cannot show a clean record, not because the businesses are bad.

12
00:01:03,432 --> 00:01:05,970
Picture the owner of a grocery in Mirpur.

13
00:01:05,970 --> 00:01:13,586
Her money moves through bKash and Nagad, a bank account and a cash box, and her credit sales live in a paper baki register.

14
00:01:13,586 --> 00:01:18,105
She has three questions, and they are exactly the three areas of Topic E.

15
00:01:18,105 --> 00:01:21,324
Which loan is really the cheapest, and can I get it?

16
00:01:21,324 --> 00:01:25,349
Will I run short of cash, when, and what can I do about it today?

17
00:01:25,349 --> 00:01:27,763
And is my business actually doing well?

18
00:01:27,763 --> 00:01:35,688
Everything in this demo runs on five synthetic Dhaka shops with eighteen months of daily records, clearly labelled as synthetic.

19
00:01:37,188 --> 00:01:40,044
Why not just put a chatbot on top of the ledger?

20
00:01:40,044 --> 00:01:42,662
Because language models are not calculators.

21
00:01:42,662 --> 00:01:48,612
They pick the wrong figure, rarely catch their own mistakes, and sound more confident than they are.

22
00:01:48,612 --> 00:01:51,826
With money, a guessed number becomes a wrong decision.

23
00:01:51,826 --> 00:01:53,789
So DecisionGuard splits the work.

24
00:01:53,789 --> 00:01:59,620
Code computes every number with exact decimal arithmetic, and records where each number came from.

25
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,643
The model only plans and explains.

26
00:02:01,643 --> 00:02:05,868
And any number the model states is recomputed before the owner sees it.

27
00:02:07,368 --> 00:02:09,061
Here is the whole pipeline.

28
00:02:09,061 --> 00:02:16,960
The shop's own records come in: mobile-money and bank statements, the cash book, the baki register, even a photo of a receipt.

29
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,465
They become typed facts.

30
00:02:18,465 --> 00:02:26,113
Bangla and Banglish are read correctly, names and phone numbers become tokens, and every row remembers where it came from.

31
00:02:26,113 --> 00:02:29,749
Deterministic engines compute everything from those facts.

32
00:02:29,749 --> 00:02:31,693
The copilot plans and explains.

33
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:36,896
Anything that leaves DecisionGuard needs the owner's approval with a one-time code.

34
00:02:36,896 --> 00:02:42,288
And any number on any screen can be tapped to show its formula and the rows behind it.

35
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:44,974
Area B, cash flow.

36
00:02:44,974 --> 00:02:57,230
DecisionGuard forecasts thirteen weeks ahead with a thousand simulated paths, built from the shop's own weekday, month-end and Eid patterns, and from how late each customer usually pays.

37
00:02:57,230 --> 00:03:07,641
For our synthetic hardware shop, there is an 86.7 percent chance of a cash gap that starts in five days, with an expected shortfall of about 73 thousand taka.

38
00:03:07,641 --> 00:03:14,098
Every possible fix is measured on the same thousand paths, so the difference is the fix, not luck.

39
00:03:14,098 --> 00:03:23,652
The cheapest one, asking a buyer to pay early, closes almost the whole gap at no cost, and it arrives as an action card for the owner to approve.

40
00:03:25,152 --> 00:03:26,433
Area A, financing.

41
00:03:26,433 --> 00:03:36,327
Lenders quote headline rates, so DecisionGuard turns every option into dated cash flows and solves for the true yearly cost, fees included.

42
00:03:36,327 --> 00:03:46,079
The same 9 percent headline costs 11.29 percent a year as a normal bank loan, and 22.15 percent as a digital loan repaid in daily debits.

43
00:03:46,079 --> 00:03:53,411
Our catalogue holds 13 real Bangladeshi loan products, each with its source and the date we checked it.

44
00:03:53,411 --> 00:03:58,892
If a lender asks for a fact we do not hold, DecisionGuard says not on record.

45
00:03:58,892 --> 00:04:00,600
It never assumes a pass.

46
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:03,226
Area C, analysis.

47
00:04:03,226 --> 00:04:14,024
DecisionGuard builds cash-basis statements and thirteen ratios, each one clickable down to the transactions, and it compares decisions before the owner makes them.

48
00:04:14,024 --> 00:04:21,642
Here, five options for the same hardware shop are replayed on the same thousand paths across forty economic states.

49
00:04:21,642 --> 00:04:25,749
A loan barely helps, because it pays out after the gap starts.

50
00:04:25,749 --> 00:04:35,487
Offering one large customer two percent off for paying early costs 7,600 taka, and cuts the risk of dipping below the buffer from 94 to 52 percent.

51
00:04:35,487 --> 00:04:42,708
The advice held in 8 of 10 stress re-runs, and never changed when we only shuffled rows or renamed customers.

52
00:04:44,208 --> 00:04:49,978
The copilot is where most AI products cut corners, so we built five steps around the model.

53
00:04:49,978 --> 00:04:54,606
First, every question is screened for prompt injection in four languages.

54
00:04:54,606 --> 00:04:59,742
Second, a model proposes a plan, and code removes anything it does not recognise.

55
00:04:59,742 --> 00:05:06,844
The owner's own question decides what is answered first, so asking about a loan gets the loan, not every report.

56
00:05:06,844 --> 00:05:11,346
Third, every number in the answer is recomputed by an independent path.

57
00:05:11,346 --> 00:05:15,403
Fourth, a model from a different family argues the case against.

58
00:05:15,403 --> 00:05:21,744
Fifth, if checks fail or votes disagree, DecisionGuard says I don't know, and names what is missing.

59
00:05:23,244 --> 00:05:26,106
Here is something no single-shop tool can do.

60
00:05:26,106 --> 00:05:33,931
These three synthetic shops owe each other in a circle: 11.5 lakh taka of debt, with each shop waiting for the next to pay.

61
00:05:33,931 --> 00:05:40,864
Minimum-cost netting clears all of it with 1.9 lakh taka of cash, moving only along debts that already exist.

62
00:05:40,864 --> 00:05:46,017
Every owner must approve with a one-time code, and one refusal cancels the round.

63
00:05:46,017 --> 00:05:58,548
The settled record is sealed with a salted hash that can be anchored on the Ethereum Sepolia testnet, so anyone can later check it was not edited, without the chain ever seeing a name or an amount.

64
00:06:00,048 --> 00:06:04,664
Security comes down to one promise: money never moves without the owner.

65
00:06:04,664 --> 00:06:06,202
Every action has a tier.

66
00:06:06,202 --> 00:06:16,460
Anything that leaves DecisionGuard is execute tier: the owner approves that exact card with a fresh one-time code, and the policy is checked again when it runs.

67
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:20,114
Four actions are denied to everyone, including the owner.

68
00:06:20,114 --> 00:06:26,717
The audit log is a hash chain the database refuses to edit, and only anonymised text can reach a model.

69
00:06:26,717 --> 00:06:28,897
Our injection guard is rules only.

70
00:06:28,897 --> 00:06:35,244
On a fresh held-out set it caught 15 of 24 attacks and wrongly blocked 10 of 24 innocent questions.

71
00:06:35,244 --> 00:06:42,360
So we do not rely on it: an injected instruction still needs the owner's one-time code before anything happens.

72
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:47,575
Everything we show is backed by evidence you can rerun.

73
00:06:47,575 --> 00:06:52,911
More than 2,500 automated tests, and none of them calls a model or the network.

74
00:06:52,911 --> 00:06:59,327
A sandbox log of 48 steps through the real API, from sign-in to an approved and audited action.

75
00:06:59,327 --> 00:07:02,705
Thirteen real loan products, each with its source.

76
00:07:02,705 --> 00:07:05,879
And the app speaks English, Bangla and Chinese.

77
00:07:05,879 --> 00:07:12,701
Every pull request runs lint, tests, dependency audits and a secret scan, then boots the whole stack.

78
00:07:12,701 --> 00:07:18,780
The evidence index in the repository lists every file and the command that regenerates it.

79
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:23,322
We want to be clear about what is not proven yet.

80
00:07:23,322 --> 00:07:27,543
All demo data is synthetic, and no real shop has used DecisionGuard.

81
00:07:27,543 --> 00:07:33,068
The injection guard is rules only, so the approval rules, not the guard, keep money safe.

82
00:07:33,068 --> 00:07:37,041
The copilot was measured offline, not with live models at scale.

83
00:07:37,041 --> 00:07:40,766
Receivables and message drafts are reduced, with no sending.

84
00:07:40,766 --> 00:07:47,843
Market prices are public lists from Bangladesh and China, as published, not live, and vendor quotes are synthetic.

85
00:07:47,843 --> 00:08:03,984
Next, we want to pilot with consenting Dhaka shops using their own bKash and Nagad exports, send approved reminders through SMS partners, bring in licensed lenders to fund netting rounds, and add a learned injection classifier with an external security review.

86
00:08:05,484 --> 00:08:10,998
DecisionGuard gives a small shop owner numbers she can check, and actions she approves.

87
00:08:10,998 --> 00:08:19,236
Code computes every figure, the copilot explains it and checks itself, and nothing that matters happens without her one-time code.

88
00:08:19,236 --> 00:08:19,870
Thank you.

89
00:08:19,870 --> 00:08:20,504
Dhonnobad.

90
00:08:20,504 --> 00:08:21,264
Shieh shieh.

91
00:08:21,264 --> 00:08:25,764
The code, the documentation and the evidence are all in our repository.

